From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 04:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ax630c: do not read the environment off the eMMC

The environment read is the first data transfer of every boot and, at
CONFIG_ENV_SIZE = 1 MiB, by far the largest one before the payload. This
board cannot afford it. Multi-block transfers do not work on its Cadence
SD4HC, so it runs with `cdns,single-block-only`, and a 1 MiB environment
is 2048 separate single-block reads before U-Boot has done anything.

One of them timing out is not recoverable, which is the part that makes
this fatal rather than slow. Measured on hardware, from a boot captured
in the pre-console buffer:

  Loading Environment from MMC... Transfer data timeout
  failed to set vqmmc-voltage to 3.3V        (nine times)
  unable to select a mode: -5
  *** Warning - No block device, using default environment
  ...
  Retrieving file: /Image
  Transfer data timeout
  Error reading cluster
  Skipping nixos for failure retrieving kernel

The re-initialisation that would clear the timeout walks
mmc_select_mode_and_width() down towards the legacy modes, and those ask
for 3.3 V I/O signalling. This board's vqmmc is a fixed 1.8 V rail, so
the switch cannot happen; the card ends with no mode selected and no
block device, and every read after that fails too. `mmc rescan` in the
boot retries cannot help, because it is the same code path.

Nothing is lost by not reading it. The whole boot is described by
CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND and CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS, which are compiled in;
the stored environment existed to carry `bootcount` and the A/B slot
name, and both of those are read and written from Linux with
fw_printenv/fw_setenv, which addresses the partition itself and is
unaffected. `bootcount` in the environment does become unavailable to
U-Boot, so a future health-gated rollback wants DM_BOOTCOUNT_SYSCON --
this SoC has exactly the sort of reset-surviving scratch register that
backend is for, and it is already the boot's evidence channel.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig b/configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig
--- a/configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig
+++ b/configs/ax630c_nanokvm_pro_defconfig
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 CONFIG_CMDLINE_PARTITION=y
 CONFIG_CMDLINE_PARTITION_DEFAULT="blkdevparts=mmcblk0:768K(spl),512K(ddrinit),256K(atf),256K(atf_b),1536K(uboot),1536K(uboot_b),1M(env),6M(logo),6M(logo_b),1M(optee),1M(optee_b),1M(dtb),1M(dtb_b),64M(kernel),64M(kernel_b),128M(boot),-(rootfs)"
 # CONFIG_EFI_PARTITION is not set
-CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
